/// `timeout`, `network_error`, `serialization_error`, `cancelled` or `_OTHER`).
/// The counter `http.client.request.count` (unit `{request}`) and the histogram
/// `http.client.request.duration` (unit `s`) carry the same attributes. The
/// instrumentation scope is the package name and its version. The hook writes
/// `traceparent` (and `tracestate`) itself, so the request names the client span
/// as its parent. Nothing records a query string, a header value or a
/// credential.
///
/// It needs the `opentelemetry` feature, and only the OpenTelemetry API: the
/// application installs the SDK. Create the hook after the global providers are
/// installed, or pass your own with [`OpenTelemetryCallHook::with_providers`].
///
/// ```rust,ignore
/// let hook = petstore::OpenTelemetryCallHook::new();
/// let config = petstore::Configuration::builder()
///     .call_hook(std::sync::Arc::new(hook))
///     .build();
/// ```
